 5. 🗳️ AI scrambles political map 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Stock: Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The search for a winning AI message is pushing candidates and lawmakers into unexpected political territory, Axios' Maria Curi writes. 

 Why it matters: AI is redrawing traditional political alliances, pitting factions of both parties against each other and creating surprising new coalitions. Three ways AI is scrambling the political map:

 Trump world vs. Tea Party on data centers. Tea Party-linked Humans First is pressing Republicans to confront growing opposition to data centers, casting it as a MAGA issue — but Trump world is keeping its distance, with administration sources saying the group has no White House influence. Centrist Democrats vs. progressives on data centers. New York Gov. Kathy Hochul and progressive state Sen. Kristen Gonzalez joined forces on the state's first-in-the-nation data center moratorium. But Gonzalez is pushing Hochul to go further with a three-year ban, testing how closely the party's two wings can align. Libertarians and progressives on surveillance. In Pennsylvania and West Virginia , Republicans are joining Democrats in pushing safeguards against government and industry misuse of AI-powered surveillance. Keep reading ... Get AI+ Government . 

 
 
