 6. 🫧 AI perception bubble 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Allie Carl/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Simon Hernandez-Arthur — the new author of Axios Communicators , our weekly newsletter covering the biggest trends in the comms industry — writes: 

 AI has become an everyday tool for communicators, but many of the audiences they're trying to reach remain deeply skeptical of how it's being used.

 Why it matters: Communicators risk getting stuck in a pro-AI bubble, where the ubiquity of the technology among colleagues and executives makes it easy to overlook the skepticism — and sometimes outright hostility — it generates. Half of U.S. consumers prefer to give their business to brands that don't use generative AI in consumer-facing messages, advertising and content, according to a Gartner survey from earlier this year.

 Younger consumers were particularly skeptical: 57% of Gen Z and millennials said generative AI has made content quality worse. Keep reading . 

 
 
