 7. ⚡ Scoop: Key national security aide leaves White House 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Andy Baker (far right) advised Vice President Vance at the Munich Security Conference last year. Photo: Johannes Simon/Getty Images White House deputy national security adviser Andy Baker is leaving the administration in the coming weeks, Axios' Barak Ravid and Marc Caputo report. 

 Why it matters: Baker, who also served as national security adviser to Vice President Vance, was among the staffers most central to the administration's foreign policy and national security decision-making over the last 18 months. Cliff Sims, who succeeded Baker as Vance's national security adviser earlier this summer, will continue in that role. Mike Needham will continue as White House deputy national security adviser.

 Baker is expected to work in the private sector with Robert O'Brien, one of President Trump's national security advisers during his first term. Share this story . 

 
 
